EFF wordlists
-------------

The link-name wordlist in core/src/words.txt is derived from the Electronic
Frontier Foundation's passphrase wordlists -- EFF Short Wordlist #1 and the
EFF Large Wordlist -- by taking a length-capped union of their base forms and
hand-curating it down. The EFF wordlists are (c) Electronic Frontier
Foundation and licensed CC-BY-3.0-US.

  Author:  Electronic Frontier Foundation
  Source:  https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2016/07/new-wordlists-random-passphrases
  License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/us/

The wordlist here is a modified subset, not a copy of either list.

BIP39 English wordlist
----------------------

The same union drew on the BIP-0039 English wordlist, published in the
bitcoin/bips repository under the MIT License.

  Source:  https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0039/english.txt


libphonenumber, via the phonenumber crate
-----------------------------------------

The `tel:` and `sms:` previews classify numbers with the `phonenumber` crate,
a Rust port of Google's libphonenumber. The crate compiles libphonenumber's
numbering-plan metadata into the server binary, so a redistributed binary
carries both.

  Crate:    https://crates.io/crates/phonenumber
  Source:   https://github.com/whisperfish/rust-phonenumber
  Upstream: https://github.com/google/libphonenumber
  License:  Apache License 2.0 (both)

Apache-2.0 is one of the two licences YuioLink itself is offered under, so
taking the Apache side of the dual grant covers the combined work. YuioLink's
own code stays dual MIT/Apache-2.0.


