Unicode variation sequence data
-------------------------------

server/assets/unicode/ holds three Unicode data files, embedded verbatim in
the server binary so a registered variation sequence (an emoji style, a
registered kanji glyph) is not mistaken for a hidden character. Each is pinned
by SHA-256 in server/src/variation.rs.

  StandardizedVariants.txt       Unicode 18.0.0 Character Database
  emoji-variation-sequences.txt  Unicode 18.0.0 Character Database
  IVD_Sequences.txt              Ideographic Variation Database, 2026-08-03

  Copyright (c) 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc.
  License:    Unicode License v3, server/assets/unicode/LICENSE.txt
  Source:     https://www.unicode.org/Public/18.0.0/ucd/
              https://www.unicode.org/ivd/data/2026-08-03/
